{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>It shall guide you</b> — so that your foot does not strike a stone." "<b>It shall guard</b> — for you cannot guard yourself at the time of your slumber." "<b>And you shall awaken</b> — and the sense is: even if there is no speech in your mouth when you awaken." "<b>It shall speak with you</b> — so that you not be afraid."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:21:13.628128006Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}